  "fanTake": "Well, that was thoroughly unspectacular in the best way possible. The Patriots muscled out a 20-3 win over Pittsburgh on Sunday—a defensive clinic that makes you grateful we have a defense, even if our offense is still searching for the rhythm that carried us through last year. R. Stevenson was the game's most impactful player by win probability added, which tells you everything about how this game unfolded: methodical, grinding, not exactly must-see TV but undeniably effective. Sure, we're not lighting it up on offense yet, but when you're holding the Steelers to field goal, you don't need brilliance—you just need to keep showing up."
